.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt SVCCTL 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm svcctl
.Nd control RavenBSD services
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm status Ar name
.Nm
.Cm start Ar name
.Nm
.Cm stop Ar name
.Nm
.Cm restart Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility talks to
.Xr init 8
through the
.Dq svc:
control scheme.
Every command prints one line per service:
.D1 Ar name state restarts
where
.Ar state
is one of
.Dq stopped ,
.Dq starting ,
.Dq running ,
.Dq restarting ,
.Dq failed
or
.Dq gave-up ,
and
.Ar restarts
is the current restart count.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "restart"
.It Cm list
List every service.
.It Cm status Ar name
Print the current state of
.Ar name .
.It Cm start Ar name
Start a stopped service.
.It Cm stop Ar name
Terminate the service process with the authorized termination primitive and wait until it has
reached terminal state, its scheme name is released and its worker has observed the exit.
.It Cm restart Ar name
Stop the service and start a fresh instance after the old process is gone; the replacement cannot
race the old scheme name.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A successful command exits 0.
A usage error, an unknown service, a malformed status line or a failed control
request exits 1 with
.Dq svcctl: <name>: <message>
on standard error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr init 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
